from pathlib import Path
r=Path('/home/bobywoby/eecs553/deliverables')
(r/'sections/00_summary.tex').write_text(r'''\paragraph{Scope of Reproducibility.}
Diffusion Forcing claims stable video rollout beyond the training horizon, improved Maze2D planning reward and a reweighted ELBO \cite{chen2025diffusion}. This draft audits the released main implementation and expands the proof. Minecraft inference has begun; long-horizon and Maze2D results remain pending. Franka robotics and time series are excluded.
\paragraph{Methodology.}
We use upstream commit \texttt{475e0bcab87545e48b24b39fb46a81fe59d80594}, released pretrained checkpoints and inference-only instrumentation. The actual device is an RTX 4090 Laptop GPU with 16 GB VRAM. No training was performed. The first completed inference used 0.12223 GPU-hours; metric postprocessing used 0.00085 GPU-hours, separate from 0.00115 setup diagnostic GPU-hours. An additional rollout is in progress and is not included in those completed-job totals.
\paragraph{Results.}
The one-times Minecraft run produced eight ten-frame videos. Mean generated-transition MSE was $0.01313\pm0.00648$ and LPIPS was $0.1433\pm0.0543$ (standard deviations across video means). This short-horizon result does not test extrapolation. Long-horizon stability, planning and sampling-scheme differences remain \textbf{[TBD]}. The theoretical audit reconstructs the intended ELBO while identifying sign and indexing discrepancies in the printed appendix.
\paragraph{What was easy.}
Once the quickstart archive was available, the released checkpoint loaded and produced finite video tensors. The paper source enabled checking figure provenance, configurations and proof steps; source figures are prepared for comparisons.
\paragraph{What was difficult.}
Initial restricted execution hid the GPU; device access now works without driver changes. Legacy MuJoCo needed local headers and compiler compatibility flags; both mazes now pass reset/step and dataset-loading checks. The video checkpoint records 110,000 steps, versus 100,000 in the README. Released attention and sliding-window rollout differ from the paper's RNN, while maze settings and metrics changed and MCG is absent.
\paragraph{Communication with original authors.}
Correspondence is unconfirmed. Questions for the authors concern robot data, the teacher-forcing baseline and Table 1 evaluation.
''')
